 ### Fixed
 
+- **References respect unknown receivers.** Finding usages or renaming a member on an untyped receiver no longer selects same-named members from unrelated classes. Macro registration searches also exclude unrelated or unknown call chains. Known typed and framework receivers keep their scoped results. Contributed by @longdo
+
 - **Nested Composer projects keep independent completion and PHP settings.** Opening a containing Composer workspace also discovers its child projects. Installed libraries retain the consuming application's configuration, and saved manifest changes preserve current unsaved buffers. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
 
 - **Composer projects keep their own symbols and PHP settings.** Completion and navigation distinguish apps that use the same class, function or constant names. Unsaved edits to a shared dependency follow its active source without replacing another open buffer's text. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
